cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use radar.raman, please cite the paper below."
type: software
title: "radar.raman: Raman Spectral Analysis Using Deep Learning for Artifact Removal"
abstract: "An R implementation of the RADAR method. Decomposes Raman spectra into
  baseline, cosmic rays, noise and Raman peaks using bundled pretrained standard and
  ensemble convolutional networks. Neural network inference, automatic
  differentiation, training, synthetic data generation, evaluation and spectral file
  conversion are implemented entirely in R."
version: 0.1.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/bogdanoancea/R-RADAR"
keywords:
  - Raman spectroscopy
  - spectral decomposition
  - baseline correction
  - cosmic ray removal
  - denoising
  - deep learning
  - convolutional neural network
  - R
